{"work_id":"tirumbippaar","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":45,"scene_status":"verified","unit_count":27,"units":[{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u001","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":58,"printed_page":50}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(The mill owner and Usha.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u002","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d001","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":58,"printed_page":50}]},"translation":{"english_text":"I heaved a sigh of relief thinking one fellow was gone. Now another one sprouts up—Pandiyan."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u003","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d002","speaker_label":"ஊஷா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":58,"printed_page":50}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Can you think everyone is like Paranthaman and knock them down with money? People firm in their ideals will not bow their heads before the safe, Appa!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u004","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d003","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Keep quiet, Usha! You don't know anything!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u005","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d004","speaker_label":"ஊஷா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"What, Appa? Is it your opinion that a lady doctor knows nothing about the world?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u006","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d005","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Lady doctor!... These workers keep tormenting me with 'workers, workers' and cause me losses running into thousands. Can you give medicine for that mental anguish?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u007","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d006","speaker_label":"ஊஷா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Oh! I can. But this medicine must be placed on the leaf called the heart, mixed with the honey called compassion, and taken. Do you know the name of the medicine, Appa? Social justice. Equality. It will taste a little bitter at first. Then it will become all right."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u008","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d007","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Usha!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u009","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d008","speaker_label":"ஊஷா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Why are you getting angry? Attend to the workers' grievances. Everything will settle down."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u010","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(The peon enters.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u011","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d009","speaker_label":"பியூன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Pandiyan too has come to see you."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u012","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d010","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Pandiyan! Tell him to come! Tell him to come! Did you see, Usha? These fellows put on the costume of leaders only to hunt for money."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u013","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Pandiyan enters.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u014","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d011","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Sitting down) I came about an important matter...."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u015","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d012","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Tell me...."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u016","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d013","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"The workers."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u017","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d014","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51}]},"translation":{"english_text":"I know. Ask for however much money you want to suppress them; I'll give it."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u018","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d015","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":59,"printed_page":51},{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Sir! I am not Paranthaman, who thunders, 'The owner on the bed—the worker in famine,' and then gets caught in bribery. I am Pandiyan—a comrade of the workers....","notes":["This source-labelled utterance crosses PDF 59→60 and remains one English unit.","The Tamil deliberately plays on `மஞ்சம் / பஞ்சம் / லஞ்சம்`; the semantic contrast is preserved, but the exact sound pattern cannot be reproduced naturally in English."]}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u019","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d016","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Pandiyan, listen to me."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u020","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d017","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"I need not listen to your words. You pay attention to the sighs of those who labour!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u021","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d018","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Sighs, labour, sweat, blood—I've heard all this so much that my ears are blocked!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u022","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d019","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Your ears will become blocked, your eyes will go dark, your mouth will close. Your hands will stop moving! In the end, even your heart will stop. I am warning you so that such a pitiable state does not come about."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u023","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d020","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Hey, did you come here to deliver a sermon?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u024","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d021","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"No. Seeing how far the condition of the workers has fallen behind, I came to lament with a wounded heart."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u025","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d022","speaker_label":"முதலாளி","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Go to the cremation ground if you want to lament."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u026","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s045-d023","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"You man of luxury! Remember this."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s045-u027","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":60,"printed_page":52}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Pandiyan leaves. The mill owner paces about angrily.)"}}]}